#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Run the orca-kit:spec-review hard gates on a spec.

Usage:
  gate [--repo ROOT] <spec.md> [<spec.md> ...]
  gate --gates

  --repo ROOT   The repo the spec belongs to: where .orca-kit/spec-review.yml
                is read from and where a block's local "$schema" path is
                resolved. Defaults to the nearest directory at or above the
                spec that contains .orca-kit/ or .git.
  --gates       List the gates and their rules, and exit.

Gates, in order (docs/spec-review/ROADMAP.md, v0.2):
  check     skills/spec/check --as accepted, run as a subprocess.
  secrets   No credentials or personal data anywhere in the file.
  blocks    Every fenced json / yaml / openapi block parses; OpenAPI
            documents have their required fields, and a block naming a
            local "$schema" file validates against it.
  trace     The spec names a ticket, when the repo config sets ticket_pattern.
  length    The spec body is within the word ceiling (max_words).

Prints one line per problem, in the spec checker's format:
  <file>:<line>: <error|warning> [<gate>.<rule>] <section>: <problem>. Fix: <what to do>.
then one result line per file:
  <file>: gates ok: check, secrets, blocks, trace, length
  <file>: gates failed: <gate> (<n>), ...; passed: <gate>, ...

Every gate is deterministic: the same spec and config always give the same
output. Warnings never fail a gate.

Exit codes: 0 every gate passes, 1 a gate fails, 2 a usage error, an
unreadable spec, a spec the checker can't parse, or an invalid config.

Repo settings, all optional, in <repo>/.orca-kit/spec-review.yml:
  ticket_pattern: '[A-Z][A-Z0-9]+-[0-9]+'   # Python regex; set = traceability required
  max_words: 2000                           # length ceiling, words in the body
  secret_patterns:                          # extra secret regexes (Python)
    - 'acme_[a-z0-9]{32}'
The file is YAML in the subset described at parse_yaml below; any other key,
or a value of the wrong type, is a config error (exit 2).

Python 3 standard library only; no install step.
"""

